-- examples/checks/asks-derived.rofl — AN ask CONCLUDED BY A RULE KEEPS EVERY RULE.
-- dv_a is asked as a fact and dv_b by a rule. What a world asks is read before its rules run, so a derived ask cannot
-- choose them: a rule concluding asks keeps every rule (said in the diagnostics), and dv_b is answered, where a cone
-- of dv_a alone would leave it out.
asks(dv_a).
edb(dv_src).
dv_src(1).
asks(dv_b) :- dv_src(1).
dv_a(X) :- dv_src(X).
dv_b(X) :- dv_src(X).
-- expect-row: dv_b[main](1)
-- expect-row: asks[main](dv_b)
